hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18535","Abd al-Samad and Affan said: Hammam narrated to us, Qatadah narrated to us, from Hanzalah the scribe, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever guards the five prayers, their bowing, their prostration, their ablution, and their times, and knows they are true from Allah, will enter Paradise, or he said: Paradise becomes due for him."
"18536","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us, Sa'id narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Hanzalah al-Usaydi, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever guards the five prayers, their ablution, their times, their bowing, and their prostration, regarding them as a right of Allah upon him, will be forbidden to the Fire."
